The write tests use SonicBoom 4.2.1 against real local files. They intercept only the Node
fs.write callback to reproduce a delayed write, a partial write, and EIO. The partial case then
uses the original fs.write for both the first fragment and remainder and checks writtenBytes
against the real file size. The EIO case checks safe-code-only failure state and actual fd release.
